---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About the Alma Consort — a professional chamber choir in London directed by Luca Wetherall and Izzy Mohan.">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      The Alma Consort is a professional chamber choir drawn from some of London's most accomplished young singers. Founded with a shared commitment to musical precision and expressive depth, the ensemble performs across a wide-ranging repertoire — classical, contemporary, jazz, and popular music — in concert and in the recording studio.
    </p>

    <p>
      The ensemble maintains its own in-house audio and video production capability, allowing recordings to be produced to a consistently high standard whether in a studio setting or on location.
    </p>

    <p>
      Through the <strong>Alma Scholars</strong> programme, the Consort is dedicated to mentoring the next generation of young choral singers.
    </p>

    <hr class="bio-divider" />

    <div class="bio">
      <p>
        <strong>Luca Wetherall</strong> is a conductor, singer, and pianist. He is Director of Music and Organist at St Mary's Acton and Choral Director at St John the Baptist, Holland Road. A Clarendon Scholar at the University of Oxford, his doctoral research explores popular music, and he serves as a Tutor at the Faculty of Music. As a singer, Luca performs regularly with leading ensembles in London and beyond. His conducting brings a scholarly depth to programming and an instinct for drawing expressive, finely balanced sound from choral forces of every size.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bio">
      <p>
        <strong>Izzy Mohan</strong> is a pianist, conductor, and singer. She is Director of Music at St Mary's Harrow-on-the-Hill, where she directs the choral and organ programme. A graduate of the University of Oxford with a First Class degree, Izzy holds a Master of Music from the Royal Academy of Music, where she was awarded the Ruth Harte Scholarship. She has performed at the Royal Festival Hall, the Austrian Cultural Forum, and the Oxford International Song Festival. Her musicianship combines a pianist's sensitivity to texture and colour with a conductor's clarity of intention.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .bio-divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(60, 60, 60, 0.15);
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .bio {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bio strong {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
</style>
